    <script type="application/ld+json" id="bv-jsonld-reviews-data">
      {"@type":"Product","review":[{"datePublished":"2024-08-26T22:15:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-26T21:49:25.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Tony2toes"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Upgraded from my Watch 5 Pro the new Ultra is definitely a big improvement. The Ultra is so much quicker and less laggy. I consider it up to today's standards for a smart watch. The Galaxy AI feature on the Ultra is cool with the sleep score. It also gives you an idea of your energy score by using your previous day activities and sleep score to let you know what how your body is. \n\nBattery run time between the Watch 5 Pro and Ultra is about the same (well they both have the battery capacity). \n\nSo far we have 2 Watch Ultras for me and the wife. We both love it compared to our W5P.","video":[{"contentUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d0oqE2MykXI","thumbnail":{"@type":"ImageObject","name":"www.youtube.com"},"uploadDate":"2024-08-26T21:49:25.000+00:00","@type":"VideoObject","name":"d0oqE2MykXI","description":"Review video send by user","thumbnailUrl":"https://img.youtube.com/vi/d0oqE2MykXI/hqdefault.jpg"}],"headline":"Ultra is really Ultra!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-14T23:45:06.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-10-14T23:24:31.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Moobert"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] First this ultra has the best battery life...almost 48hrs! I only use wifi and Bluetooth. I don't use cellular cause my phone is always with me or within range to find. The AI that is used for heart rate is not noticeable, but I do notice an improvement with accuracy and the speed of measurement. This watch recognizes exercises and is more attentive to movements. \n\nNow, the only negative I have to say is the mirror finish is still on the metal edges of this watch and will be distracting for some drivers. I have a cover on mine to reduce scratches and to cover the shiny parts.\n\nOverall, I enjoy this watch with the new stretch bands and colors.","headline":"Great battery!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-09-08T11:30:06.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-08T11:03:32.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"EdogElite"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Great watch!\nGreat size.  It is large, but it blends in.  It is smooth when using multiple features.  The screen size helps with reading or when calling someone. \nThe watch bands can be switched out easily and quickly.  I like the push button lock.  I have three different styles and colors.  You can customize for your day or event. \nThe volume is loud and I specifically like the emergency alert ping.  I am a hunter, and I can see the need to alert for help at times.  This in line with the track back feature in the hiking app really helps a person get back on track or get out of unfamiliar territory.  Hell, it could just be a parking spot.  Lol","headline":"This watch is bold","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T22:00:05.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T21:31:21.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Stevep"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I upgraded to the 7 Ultra from my 4 classic. Thought I would miss the bezel but so far it hasn't bothered me. Everything about the ultra has just impressed me and functions so much smoother than I was expecting. Seen alot of reviews talking about the weight and size but also don't even notice it. I also love the locks for the wrist band. Makes it so easy to switch bands when I need to put the case on it to keep it protected at work then switch to the normal band on my days off. The battery life has been a huge upgrade. With always on I have been getting over 2 days. Cant wait to see what improvements they come up with for the next model Ultra.","headline":"Such a great watch","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-28T17:30:06.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-28T13:11:05.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"andymcn"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I recently upgraded to the Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra, and it's been a game-changer. The most notable improvements over the previous generation are the significantly enhanced battery life and the much brighter screen. I can easily get through a couple of days on a single charge, which is fantastic for my busy lifestyle. The screen brightness is another standout feature, making it much easier to see notifications and apps even in bright sunlight. Overall, the Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra feels like a substantial upgrade, offering a seamless blend of performance and convenience. Highly recommended for anyone looking to upgrade their smartwatch!","headline":"Great upgrade over previous Samsung watches","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-04-06T05:45:07.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-04-03T23:46:49.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"TheWorkOutAnimall1090"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I love everything about the Galaxy. Watch ultra, the battery\nThe apps, the smoothness of the touch of the screen, the buttons. My favorite part of the Galaxy Watch is the band please continue to make more bands like that. It's stretchy, comfortable, dries, fast from water, just all around great. When you talk on the phone from your watch, the sound is great. The funny part is when it's time for my son to go to bed. He plays with my watch and watches YouTube from you. My watch He's something else but I love the watch. The watch is great and my son loves his well.While it's on my wrist, but thanks.Samsung continue to make watches like this, please","headline":"My love for galaxy watch ultra and my son. Lol","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-11-30T20:00:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-11-30T19:41:46.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Rich"},"reviewBody":"I found the watch to a good watch with at least a 3 day battery supply. I am still learning more features as I countinue to use it as compared to a Samsung Gear 3 that I had before. Biggest difference in the learning curve is the watch face and how well it adapts for me. My biggest complaint on the purchasing experience is that you need a USB-C charger adapter to be able to charge the phone and it does not come with the watch so you now have to go and purchase one if you do not have one already. I am not talking about the actual magnetic charger, but the adapter part that you plug a USB-C plug into that then plugs into a regular 110v a/c outlet.","headline":"Good watch, doesn't include a/c charging adapter!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-23T16:30:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-10-23T16:05:29.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Kenneth O"},"reviewBody":"Definitely a significant/noticeable upgrade on the 5 PRO that I traded in. Its quite an apparent uptick in the look, performance of this watch over the 5 PRO. Thought I'd find the orange strap and coloring on the watch a bit jarring but the best way to counter that misgiving is that its best to view the watch in person. Given that I'm bit taller than average, the larger size of the watch fits me perfectly as the 5 PRO was a touch small for me me. I don't even miss the rotating bezel. Its not perfect as the battery life could be a tad better, but its important to mess with the respective settings and features to get the desired batter life.","headline":"Definite Upgrade over the 5 Pro.","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-29T20:30:18.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-29T20:02:27.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Storm2966"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The Galaxy Watch Ultra is hands down the best smartwatch. As a retail employee that sales smart watches this watch easily stands above the rest. I previously had the Galaxy Watch 5. This watch is a huge upgrade over the Galaxy Watch 5. Among all of the improvements I think the battery is the most impressive. The Galaxy Watch Ultra arrived almost a week ago and I've only had to charge it twice. Once when I turned on the device for the first time and the second time today (one week later). I also greatly appreciate the new Galaxy AI features. In particular the energy score feature which tells me exactly how I can improve my energy and sleep.","headline":"Easily the Best Smart Watch","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2026-07-08T16:58:35.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-23T23:13:46.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"marcotjokro"},"reviewBody":"Pre-ordered the watch after the announcement and I would say I'm not disappointed. The massive 47mm size matches my hand better compared to the usual 44mm Galaxy Watch 6.\r\nThe battery lasts almost full 2 days before I need to charge (Based on usual usage: notifications, short calls, usual watch usage, auto track exercise, continuous sensor tracking).\r\nFeels more premium with the titanium material. I used it during sleep and wasn't bothered by it since I'm used to wearing a smartwatch during my sleep, although I felt it on the first day, but got used to it very fast.\r\nThe screen is very bright and vibrant and moving from app to app is very snappy.","headline":"Very bright display and very snappy performance","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-12T19:00:14.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-12T18:34:21.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"UltraFab"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I have had the Samsung Galaxy Ultra Watch for a month now. And I am incredibly ecstatic! \n\nI thought I would get decent body measurements. NOPE!\n\nThey are surreal! It's like Galaxy AI is actively transmitting data from my body to the device. Real-time heart rate, breathing exercises, blood pressure, oxygen levels...\n\nSleep monitoring, stress monitoring, and the list goes on.\n\nBATTERY LIFE is exceptional! Screen is crisp and so bright, and the animations are beautiful and so smooth 😎\n\nThe way watch bands pop off and snap in are seamless and effortless. The new action button is useful.\n\nI have nothing but great things to say. So impressed.","headline":"Smartest of the Smart","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-22T15:00:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-22T02:24:42.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Alessandro M."},"reviewBody":"I love this watch. I think it's one of the best ones Samsung has made so far. The only feedback that I have is the battery claims aren't anywhere near what I have been experiencing with this watch. I have to keep it on power save mode in order for me to have a couple to a few days worth of each side of it. If I don't have it in power saving mode I need to recharge it with it a day. What other piece of feedback is the watch bands are pretty pricey for the regular retail price. Was glad that I managed to get a second band at a discount. But if I ever want to change bands I think it's too cost prohibitive. Other than that I love this watch!","headline":"Great watch! Love it! Battery claims are off...","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2025-02-11T21:15:12.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-11T20:50:07.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Stockton1996"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Easy to use, comfortable fit. Comes in handy when phone isn't nearby. Being able to text and make calls is helpful when my device isn't on my person. The customization of watch faces is great cause I love to have variety. Nice, smooth display for seamless browsing and texting, provides fluid movement for scrolling. I work long hours and the battery life has been more than accommodating, lasting for at least 3 days at a time. The strong titanium casing was a gamechanger considering my work exposes me to the elements. The watch withstands bumps, scratches, and repetitive movement without taking damage and i love it. Well worth every penny.","headline":"Awesome convenience","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-02T01:30:07.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-02T01:10:26.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"SamsungFan81"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] As a dedicated Samsung enthusiast, I couldn't wait to try out the latest Galaxy Watch. Samsung has consistently delivered top-notch smartwatches, and this new model is no exception. Here’s my in-depth review after using it for a couple of weeks.\nThe new Galaxy Watch is a stellar addition to Samsung’s lineup, blending style, functionality, and performance seamlessly. It’s a fantastic choice for anyone looking to stay connected and track their health and fitness goals. As a Samsung fan, I’m thoroughly impressed with this latest release. Whether you're a tech enthusiast or just looking for a reliable smartwatch, the Galaxy Watch is worth considering.","headline":"Best watch ever","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T00:32:53.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T00:01:23.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Navy4163"},"reviewBody":"I received the ultra watch a week and a half ago. My only issue  / problem is with the sleep tracker which powers all the health data. Being a light sleeper, I will wake up in the night and get a glass of water. I did not take it out of sleeping mode or check the time. What I've experienced is when I do this, the earlier sleep time is erased and the only data I get is from when I returned to sleep to the morning. So all of the metrics are useless. This has and is been on ongoing issue. I backed off from purchasing a galaxy ring because it might read the same, only half of my sleep. I have since returned back to my Garmin epix watch for sleep data.","headline":"Beautiful,  long time  between charging","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-29T22:22:39.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-29T21:54:46.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Malibuguy16"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The sleep tracking with Galaxy AI is game changer.  It lets me know in depth detail of my sleep and plays into my Energy Score which I use to improve my overall sleep health. With the recommendations from the health help I have improved my sleep and hence how I feel throughout the day.\nThe device also works great with the new Galaxy buds that I got, they connect without any issues and I can leave my phone behind and still have access to all my music while out I'm and about.  \nThe only reason it doesn't get 5 is battery life. It does last me the day and a night but I'm having to charge at odd times to make sure I get my sleep monitored every night.","headline":"Samsung best watch yet","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T05:00:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T02:15:36.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Bluesbreaker"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Galaxy watch ultra is the ultimate watch anyone can dream about with cool & larger display with integrated Samsung AI and brighter than any other watch in the market.\n\nWith new robust additions to its design and new and improved battery and the new chip makes this watch so smooth to and flawless in it's operational power.\n\nI recommended this watch to my friends and they too loved this watch more than anything else.\n\nI believe in Samsung, in it's path breaking innovation in technology in it's team of engineers who are definitely striving hard to be in the lead with the other competitors. \n\nI was and always will be with the Samsung nation","headline":"The best watch till date","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-01T15:46:34.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-22T13:55:23.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Stevae"},"reviewBody":"Getting rid of the bezel was NOT a good idea from Samsung. And while I like the shape, the extremely limited customization functions of the three buttons is ridiculous and hurts the usefulness of the watch. Especially when you DOUBLED the price, without doubling the features and functions!!! The bands should be magnetic instead of this antiquated lock. While I do like the new attachment function for the bands, there aren't nearly enough choices of different bands to make it a really useful feature. WHY IS THERE EKG, BUT NO BLOOD PRESSURE function in the USA?????? It's moronic to not be able to do blood pressure, but you can do EKG. Come on Samsung!","headline":"This is NOT worth DOUBLE THE PRICE!!!!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3}},{"datePublished":"2025-08-16T13:22:46.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-08-04T22:55:06.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"pudensky"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] the Galaxy Watch Ultra, is a real head-turner. With its sturdy titanium frame, super bright display, and a ton of health and fitness features, it’s made for adventure and performance. just want a reliable companion for my daily life, this watch delivers speed, reliability, and style.\n\nThe new Quick Button and emergency siren are actually pretty handy, and the upgraded chip makes everything feel super responsive. Battery life is decent, around 2–3 days, though not quite the “Ultra” some might expect.\n it feels a bit bulky. Also, missing some features since when I am using a iphone.\n\nOverall, it’s a feature-packed, tough smartwatch with a lot to love.","headline":"Eye catching","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-29T21:30:17.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-29T21:08:20.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Charmaine"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I play music all day long at work and I'm still at about 50% when I get home. Phones are not allowed on the floor where I work, so having a smartwatch comes in handy.\n\nI've owned just about every Samsung Galaxy watch since Galaxy Watch 3, and this Ultra is the best by far. The AI features are an amazing bonus.\n\nThe siren feature is a must-have for any woman. You never know when you're going to need it. It's nice to have it just in case.\n\nSleep tracker is much, much better because it works with the new feature to measure your energy level throughout the day. The watch will also check to see if you may have sleep apnea.\n\nGreat new watch!","headline":"Battery life is amazing","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-02-13T16:15:20.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-11T23:24:46.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"LoveSamsungUltra"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I love this Galaxy Watch. I use it in every way possible aside from telling time and date. \nI have better control of health thanks to all the apps and gadgets embedded in it. My heart rate, sleeping patterns, and stress levels assist me in staying in my best through out the day.\n\nThe gestures are great to cancel a call or stop an alarm without distractions or hesitation, I simply pinch twice.\n\nScreen customizations are possible, different colors, and set ups which makes the watch screen looking unique. \n\nAnd the 3 side buttons, a simple and easy way to get some of those apps going by simply clicking on it, and those buttons are customizable as well.","headline":"User-friendly gadgets and apps","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-08-21T09:27:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-08-19T19:05:05.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"usan14"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] As being Previous Watch 6 Classic user, Watch ultra design design in photos was not that attractive but when watch arrived and used, love it, it is more bright, more fast and more spacious screen. Multiple sports activities are great. Design looks great on the wrist. Surprisingly, being little thick design watch is very light weight. Only thing which really let down was the straps received with the watch, orange colour is not a every day use colour. It looks great but may be only leisure time but to use it daily where smart casual looks required, wouldn't recommend orange colour. I really wished if there was a grey/black colour strap come with watch.","headline":"Great Looks, Quick, Sharp Display, S Health 👌","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-03-04T04:00:41.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-10T15:15:11.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"TDSC"},"reviewBody":"The watch is pretty much the Galaxy Watch 7 in a different case with an action button. It's advertised as a tough and rugged version of outdoor sports. Suddenly, one day, the sensors stopped functioning, and then the action button wasn't responding; I am now facing repair costs because it is considered out of warranty for some unseen internal damage. There is no cracked screen, no scratches or nicks. It's never been dropped and slammed against anything, yet somehow, there is damage to the motherboard. I am quickly getting fed up with Samsung, trying to avoid costs at my expense. \n\nSo think twice if you invest in this watch for its rugged, tough case.","headline":"Not really as advertised","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":2}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-07T08:47:07.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-05T13:30:12.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"usan14"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] As being Previous Watch 6 Classic user,  Watch ultra design design in photos was not that attractive but when watch arrived and used, love it, it is more bright, more fast and more spacious screen. Multiple sports activities are great. Design looks great on the wrist.\nSurprisingly, being little thick design watch is very light weight.\nOnly thing which really let down was the straps received with the watch, orange colour is not a every day use colour. It looks great but may be only leisure time but to use it daily where smart casual looks required, wouldn't recommend orange colour. I really wished if there was a grey/black colour strap come with watch.","headline":"Everything is Great Except Straps","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-13T21:15:12.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-06-13T06:08:51.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"TheRob"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I really, really like this watch. I used to be a g shock man, but this watch is really cool. It does everything my phone does, please? Music tells me where I'm at gives me directions home. I talked to it like I talked to my phone. Super cool I use it every day. I have high blood pressure. It checks my heart ekg. It checks the time I sleep. The time I wake up Tracks, everything, all in all of this thing is, my daily use. Go to and the battery life is amazing.It's like two and a half 3 days battery life!! If you want a durable, long-lasting Galaxy phone.This is the way to go!! I highly recommend to anyone looking for a new watch piece!","headline":"Galaxy watch Ultra","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-14T22:30:06.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-10-14T22:14:18.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Roobs"},"reviewBody":"First off, this watch model has grown on me. Initially, I was wasn't digging how close it looked to its competitions but the minor differences started to make it stand out much more. The grey color is classic and sleek. \r\n\r\nSecondly, the hardware itself is super responsive. No lag whatsoever after 3 weeks of use. The sleep tracking and also giving me a energy score to start my day puts me on the right track. \r\n\r\nWhat I don't like? \r\nFirstly, the price is high. \r\nsecondly, the wear os does not let me use apps like Facer to put custom watch faces that I've been using for over 5 years. Disappointing when I got this and couldn't install.","headline":"Extremely responsive and stylish.","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2025-03-31T20:45:11.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-03-27T01:45:56.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"ShaADdoWs"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Being able to not have my phone in my hands at all times is a great help for me specially at work due to sometimes having thing in my hands and not being able to put things down to check what the text message that I just received says. The seamless connection between devices and the responsiveness of the watch is unparalleled to the last generation and that of the competition, not to mention the compliments I get about how sleek and yet robust the design is. 10 out of 10 in my book. Having my center button as my key to activate the flashlight in the watch is also a life savior for whenever I'm looking for my TV remote in the dark 😅.","headline":"Great Response and Ease of Use!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-09-15T14:43:18.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-09-12T18:55:04.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"viktorija135"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The Galaxy Watch Ultra is a solid step forward for Samsung. It’s built tough with a titanium frame and a bright, crisp display that’s easy to read outdoors. Fitness tracking is reliable, and the new Quick Button makes switching workout modes super convenient.\n\nBattery life holds up well for a full day of use, though heavy users might want more. It’s a bit chunky on the wrist, but that adds to its rugged feel. If you’re into outdoor adventures or serious training, this watch won’t disappoint—especially if you’re already using a Samsung phone.\n\nOverall, it’s a powerful and stylish smartwatch that blends durability with smart features.","headline":"Great for outdoors","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-05T17:00:19.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-03T19:43:18.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Taylor"},"reviewBody":"Just bought this, took a bit to recieve, but not letting that get to me!! Absolutely love it :) I should have never upgraded from my watch 5 pro to the 6 classic, BIGGEST waste of money, EVER! BUT when the 7 ultra came out, I was MORE than ready. \n\nLittle lady of 5'3 here, and some small wrists, I see all these \"manly\" comments. BUT for my ladies it fits good! It looks so good and nice. Works great with workouts and tracking steps, and looks cute with the band I have :) \n\nBand is ADJUSTABLE! Gotta read the instructions and what not. \n\nBattery is decent, trying to let it settle into my activities before I really dis the battery life.","headline":"For ladies too!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-12-26T20:05:21.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-02T01:10:35.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"JayAndel"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I use my watch as an extension of my phone. It's a great companion to the galaxy phone. I have a panic disorder so it helps keep track of my heart rate, and if you leave your phone at home you can still use the watch to message. I actually left my phone on the way to the gym and was able to message my partner so I could get it. I do like the Galaxy AI features also. It's nice yo have live translate when you travel or have Galaxy AI help you find what you need. I also have the Galaxy buds 3 pro to help with call translations and such. All in all, they are great to have and use in every day life. Looking forward to the S25 Ultra soon!","headline":"Great features and excellent phone companion","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-28T13:30:07.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-28T10:29:06.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Alirazazaki"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I recently got my hands on galaxy watch ultra and guess what I’m amazed by it’s interesting new AI features and battery life. It is a very durable watch, bright and look great on my wrist. It does my health and fitness tracking. It monitors my heart rate, ECG, blood pressure measurements and sleep tracking. It does my step counts. I can personalise my watch dial. I can change the wrist bands to match it to any occasion. I love the feature when it makes me stand up and walk because I work in the office and I’m mostly sitting in front of the computer. I can use hand gestures to operate my watch as well.  I would definitely recommend.","headline":"AI smart","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-12-09T01:10:58.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-12-06T23:21:34.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Tubalou"},"reviewBody":"I bought this as part of the Black Friday promotion to replace my Watch 5 Pro. I was looking for some of the additional sensor capabilities and accuracy. I do like the ease of changing bands and found inexpensive adapters that allowed using the 20mm bands from my former watches. \n\nThe screen looks great and it is responsive. However, after wearing it for a day I had to return it. It was so heavy that it actually hurt my wrist and started to make my hand numb. It also won't work with the watch faces I bought for my earlier watch, but I could have lived with that.  I really wanted to like this, but I'm sticking with my 5 Pro for now.","headline":"Too heavy and uncomfortable","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-16T00:45:06.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-16T00:19:30.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Dad2JTK"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I purchased this watch to replace the Galaxy Watch Pro 5.   Good move by me.  I loved my previous Watch and basically wanted to update for a better health readings and well it also had to have a same or better battery.   I don't even know how to explain it.  But this watch seems.to work much better overall than Old Watch Pro 5.   I mentioned to friends too.  Whatever AI is in this watch in conjunction with the Samsung Ultra 24 phone i have not touched on it much yet.   I wish the BP part would work in the USA.   But I understand you can thank the FDA for not allowing that yet.  Amazing considering a galaxy watch active could do it.","headline":"Great Large Watch and has nice smooth operation","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-29T23:00:15.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-29T22:30:40.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Bosshoss"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I have owned almost all of the Galaxy watches released.  There was a period of time recently where the battery life and use of the device wasn't as good as it used to be.  I gave the Ultra a shot and so far have been blown away.  It's is very fast, responsive, loud, and best of all, the battery life has been amazingly.  I can easily get 2 full days of decent use including sleep tracking and some workouts.  I haven't had a chance to use all the Galaxy AI features yet but so far it's been good, definitely heading in the right direction.  The size is great, and fits perfectly in my wrist, and the orange band looks really good.  Highly recommend this watch!","headline":"Best Galaxy watch yet!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-07T02:15:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-07T01:59:26.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"UltraWatchLover"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] It was time to upgrade my device and I chose the ultra. I was used to larger watches so this one was a no brainer.\n\nThe functions on the watch are phenomenal! It was even able to detect symptoms of sleep apnea. I was skeptical about wearing it to bed because i thought it would be uncomfortable but I had no problems. There are multiple exercises on it and it prompts me to move around when I've been sitting too long. I have a few health issues so the watch is great in helping me monitor my heart rate. I'm also able to keep up with messages as needed.\n\nOver all, this was a good choice. I've only had it a week but I'm excited to learn more about the device.","headline":"I love it!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-02-11T23:30:11.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-11T20:18:54.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Lespaulman72"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I recently upgraded from a Galaxy watch 4 to the new Galaxy Watch Ultra and couldn't be more pleased. From the new easier to swap watch band to the large ergonomic face the Ultra is hands down the best on the market! The information I would have had to scroll through on my Watch 4 to find is now all on the first screen. Health and fitness goals, stress levels, time/date, battery level, weather information and a compass all on the face with many other options to configure to your needs and liking. Watch faces are easier to obtain with more choices also. A stylish look with larger buttons and a quicker response for device wake up are all much appreciated.","headline":"I'd be lost without it.","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-21T17:45:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-10-21T16:04:21.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Guzman reviews"},"reviewBody":"My 1st smart watch ever. Its a little big but i really like it. The band not so much its not that flexible and wont sit nice on the wireless charger i have to put something ontop of it to make sure it charges over night. Dont know if its the charger or watch but if its the watch the housing needs to be redesigned to allow use of wireless chargers. Many features. i dont trully know how to use it 100% yet but am learning samsung sends updates every know and then. So far i love the ease of use. Am a blue collar worker so not having to take my phone out of my pocket with very dirty or greasy hands its great i just look at my wrist when i get a notification.","headline":"1st time smart watch owner","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-09T23:11:00.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-04T16:25:09.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Barbara959"},"reviewBody":"I love the features but it is WAY bigger than my galaxy classic 4 which was 46mm and this is only 47mm! Also I ABSOLUTELY HATE the band that came with it!! It's either too tight or too loose. There's no happy place and it's extremely frustrating and uncomfortable. I have pretty average size wrists and measured and went with the appropriate band size as i was right in the middle of the md/lrg size. I can't wait for more bands to be released to see if that will help, that is if I decide to keep it because it's enormous and expensive. Plus why is it that I cannot access FB messenger on this watch but yet it tells me my temperature?!?","headline":"Mixed and really unsure for the amount I spent","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-02T14:15:12.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-02T13:48:06.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"PH73EX"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I was skeptical about buying something new but after receiving and setting up the watch it really changed my thoughts. The setup was simple all my previous settings linked up directly from my old watch. The battery life is exceptionally well, it last all day without needing to be charged. The health monitors in this watch are amazing tracking sleep, a snore detection, heart rate and overall health. I can track a multitude of exercises throughout the day. The display and backlight is exceptional clear and the faces give you many options to display on the watch. Can't wait to upgrade to the S24 Ultra soon to get the full experience.","headline":"Best Watch Device!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-01-15T00:15:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-01-14T23:25:16.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jon H"},"reviewBody":"I traded in the first generation Galaxy watch for this one. It is as advanced as you might expect. Easy to learn and personalize. Lots of nice features. I would give it 5 stars, except the battery is disappointing. My old watch, even after 8 years, would still go from 6am until 10 pm the next night. I thought the new watch would have a better battery, but it only lasted about 28 hours before it went into power saving, and shut off completely about 7pm the second night. Perhaps my expectations were unrealistic, but I thought it would last longer than an 8 year old watch. Other than that, I do love everything else about this watch.","headline":"Great watch.","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2025-01-01T07:48:41.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-28T05:27:38.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Posemumu"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Since smart watches have existed, I have been a demanding fan of these fascinating technologies. Always looking for comfort, versatility and above all the functionality of the device. My Galaxy Watch Ultra more than meets expectations... This Galaxy AI blew my mind. Its design makes it perfect for all my activities, the weight it carries is simply hard to believe and the speed and functionality make it unattainable. I use Bixby as my personal assistant and it is surprising how easy it is for me to make reminders, make calls, schedule the calendar and make notes instantly. In my swimming routine it becomes my assistant and I simply cannot train without it.","headline":"the best smart watch i have ever had in my life!!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-09-11T08:38:51.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-12T22:06:31.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"LZB302"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Traded my Galaxy 4 classic in on the new Galaxy ultra 7! Battery life is 3-4 days! Smooth bezel operation! Simple to transfer from classic 4 to the new Ultra 7! The finish is really nice, the Silicone band is Fantastic! Health tracking is more accurate! Speakers are better for phone usage! This is a Fantastic Smartwatch! Samsung really out did themselves on this watch! Plus the new Watch faces just for the Ultra are super, having all info you want right there on the watch face & customize it is great! Got a Battery update which may & suppose to even make battery life better, it's still updating based on my usage! Had now for over a month & simply love it!","headline":"Galaxy ultra watch 7 awesome!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T02:45:07.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T00:15:09.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Njj924"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I've used my new Galaxy Watch Ultra for about a week now. And so far it is working great.\n\nThe new health sensors seem to pick up more data and more detailed results than my previous smart watch.\n\nI haven't quite gotten used to the advanced Galaxy AI features yet.  I think it still is learning my daily habits. So I may update my review after more time with it.\n\nBut if you are looking to upgrade the ultra is awesome. Battery last longer. So far Without power saving mode on, I currently have 1 day 4hours remaining and it shows it's been 1 day and 17 hours since my last charge. So seems to be getting well over 2.5 days on a charge.","headline":"Awesome upgrade so far","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-03-19T20:15:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-03-18T05:04:00.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sammy1221"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I use the watch for sleep monitoring and counting steps.  Sometimes I will take calls with its speaker phone. \nI would like a digital display that shows heart rate clearly at all times.  This goes to HRV monitoring.  The rubber watch band is well designed.  It is always comfortable.  Heart monitoring hasn't changed.  And every night in the 4 AM or so time frame the watch has a gap in data gathering.  I've had to reconnect it a few times.  A user should probably charge it often enough to avoid power saving mode.  I should still investigate all the features..  I'm probably missing something.  If it had stronger heart analytics, it would help me with HRV etc.","headline":"Functional with room for innovation","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T05:00:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T01:21:51.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Rezzy78"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I own about 3 other watch from Samsung, and it is everything I expected, it has every function available to carry you though your day yo day  life. \nYou can wear it in your sleep, to the gym, wear it while going to the grocery store, on a hike and even swimming.\nI love the size it has a pretty sizable face 47mm,;which is way bigger from it's previous predecessors, this updated watch might not have the rotating bezel like previous watches but it make up for it with the new the 3 button design instead of the usual two.\nThe Samsung watch ultra does come with the Galaxy AI feature that is now accessible on all Samsung Galaxy Phones.","headline":"Watch Ultra","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-08-13T12:35:25.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-08-06T10:25:04.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"rwte"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I have never owned a smart watch or fitness tracker before and have been blown away by not just the look of this device, but the function and battery life too.\n\nI find the health aspects particularly good, especially sleep tracking.  It works seamlessly with my Android device and I regularly get two days out of it.  It charges quickly too so I'll often put it on in the morning so I have it for a full two days.\n\nIt is a large watch face but is not heavy.  The default band it came with is very comfortable too.  The Super AMOLED is so clean and bright.\n\nIt has exceeded every expectation, and my wife is already considering making the leap from her fitness band!","headline":"Stylish, powerful, brilliant","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-03T13:00:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-06-03T12:35:19.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Clue1970"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] This watch is my fave!  It does everything I need and more – way better than I expected. I never take it off except to charge it (wish it had Gemini instead of Google Assistant though!).  I hope you'll make a square or rectangular version someday, like the old Galaxy Gear – more screen space! That's what got me into Samsung watches in the first place.  It's gorgeous. Seriously, I got at least two or three coworkers to buy one, and my son did too!  Bigger sizes would be awesome in the future; my eyesight isn't what it used to be, and I bet a lot of us older folks, especially guys, would love a bigger watch. Also more AI features","headline":"Favorite watch so far","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-03T21:30:19.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-06-02T20:39:09.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ahboby"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I had upgraded from watch 6 to watch ultra. I absolutely love it. The AI features on the watch are awesome and works smoothly. \nThe battery life is awesome. I haven't enabled NFC all the time as it drains the battery and workout it I can use the watch without charging for couple of days easily. \nIt's a perfect size for my wrist. It does not feel heavy. The strap is long lasting and durable. \nMic works really well and speakers are loud enough to hear everything clearly.\nSetup and sync with my phone was a breeze. It's like a family and knows exactly how to interact with samsung products. I am extremely satisfied with my purchase.","headline":"Awesome battery","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-05T17:15:19.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-04T01:24:31.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Chess"},"reviewBody":"I’m upgrading from a Galaxy Watch 6 Classic. I bought the watch as I wanted more battery life and this watch does not disappoint. Mine shipped with firmware version AXFB and I’m getting 48 hours with BT on, WiFi and LTE on Auto AND AOD on.\n\nThe software is also way snappier with no lag.\n\nAlso the vibration motor got a big upgrade. It feels sort of like a PS5 Dual Sense Controller vs an N64 Rumble pack on the previous watch.\n\nLastly, I like the new band attachment system. It provides a loud positive click confirming that the band is fully seated unlike the vagueness that can sometimes happen with the usual watch band pin system.","headline":"A great upgrade from any previous Galaxy Watch","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-10T01:28:11.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-04-04T13:51:56.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Craig"},"reviewBody":"Been 6 months, worked great until 2 months ago. Now I am forced to reset and relearn the watch every few days. My wife's galaxy watch 7 (bought same time) has zero issues. So every few days, my phone and watch will disconnect, and I have to set it up again as if it's a new watch. It's frustrating, it's happened while I'm wearing the watch, on the charger, when the phone and watch are separated, last night it was the second the watch hit the charger. Reaching out to customer service today, I'm not the only one, seen a lot of this exact same problem on reddit on a variety of Samsung phones. Galaxy watch ultra paired with zflip 6","headline":"Was good, now requires constant pairing","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":1}},{"datePublished":"2025-01-08T02:30:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-01-08T01:56:07.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Gravity"},"reviewBody":"The Galaxy Watch might look bulky, but it’s surprisingly comfortable to wear, even while sleeping. After adjusting a few settings, I’m getting 2-3 days of battery life, which is solid compared to other smartwatches I’ve used.\r\n\r\nI liked how Fitbit devices could be traded in, but I wasn’t happy when the Galaxy Watch’s price dropped later during holiday sales—something to watch out for when purchasing. Performance-wise, it’s comparable to the Fitbit Ultra I had before, and while I haven’t tested its swimming or LTE features yet, I’m overall happy with its functionality and design. Once optimized, this watch is a reliable choice!","headline":"Comfortable, Reliable, and Great Battery Life","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-11-16T05:15:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-11-16T03:30:23.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Anonymous"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] A Rugged and Reliable Companion\nThe Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra is a beast of a smartwatch. Its tough, titanium build and bright, readable display make it perfect for outdoor adventures. The battery life is impressive, lasting multiple days on a single charge, and the health tracking features are comprehensive.\nWhile it might be a bit bulky for some, the extra size and weight contribute to its durability and long battery life. The watch's performance is smooth, and the customization options are plentiful. If you're an active individual who needs a reliable and feature-packed smartwatch, the Galaxy Watch Ultra is a great choice.","headline":"Amazing rugged watch with ultra battery","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-29T21:45:22.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-29T21:22:43.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Want2Like"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I finally upgraded from the original Galaxy Watch to the Watch Ultra.  There was a lot of different apps and options from the original.  Really good display and fitness tracking.  The one major complaint I have with the Watch Ultra is the battery life.  My  Galaxy Watch got 2 days out of it.  Since having the Watch Ultra for the last three days, I have only been getting just over a full day (24 hrs).  VERY disappointing for the cost of the watch.  I keep watching videos and reading threads about the Watch Ultra's battery life, and it's all over the place. \n\nSamsung, please somehow improve the battery life on my watch.\n\nThanks.","headline":"Nice upgrade, poor battery life","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-09-03T07:15:01.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-03T05:49:11.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Austin893"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] My new Galaxy Watch Ultra is without a doubt the best smart watch I've ever owned! The clarity on this beautiful screen makes my weak eyes enjoy using this practical device. I've had fun learning it's features from my previous Galaxy watch. The band is so comfortable I even forget I'm wearing it. I'm still learning the new Galaxy AI but things like voice texting, the heart rate monitor, the long battery life and ease of use have made me love Samsung even more! I brag to all my fellow Android users they need this wearable too! I learn new things everyday! Thank you for making such an amazing, dependable, feature-heavy product!","headline":"Best smart watch ever!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T15:45:16.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T15:25:30.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"REAUSTIN"},"reviewBody":"When I first seen the watch on line, I was like, Man I don't like the square body, however once I recieved the watch and started wearing it, was I wrong, I absolutely love the look.  Sure it is a little heavier than the Classic 6, does not bother me in the least. \n\nI tried out the sleep apena feature and as my wife thought it let me know that I need to speak to my DR about sleep apena.\n\nOverall the features are great, battery life for me is a little better than the Classic 6, I consider myself a moderate to heavy user.\n\nSo, was it worth the money, you bet, with the trade for the Classic 6.  If your on the fence, go for it....","headline":"Loving it,","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-29T21:15:16.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-29T20:50:13.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"ErikMN"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Samsung did it. They brought out a new watch that I couldn't refuse. The look is way more then expected. The screen is vibrant and large, great for someone like me that has vision issues. The rugged and sleek look makes me less worrysome that I have to be careful with my activity.  The smoothness of the graphics are awesome, no latency found going any activities. The connectivity has been spot on, no issues connecting to devices and remaining connected. Being transparent and honest, this is the best watch I have every had and I have had, meets all my needs and wants, and more. Thank you for listening to your customers Samsung and delivering a superiorproduct.","headline":"Wow - Samsung Watch Ultra.","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-09-09T22:00:07.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-09T14:38:07.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"RFtech53"},"reviewBody":"I really liked my 5 Pro.  But the Ultra,  in my opinion,  is a big step forward.  Mainly,  the battery life.  I've seen reviews that dis the battery.  But in my experience so far,  the Ultra's battery goes twice as long before I have to charge it.  \n\nI also like the square styling of the Ultra, as well as the new band attachment mechanism. \n\nMy only complaint is the band itself  It's too short for my wrist and I had to buy an off-brand one.  Even the OEM 5 Pro band worked on my wrist,  so I don't know why the Ultra's band is shorter. But that's okay.  I prefer metal bands anyway. I sent the OEM band back for a points credit.","headline":"A Big Improvement From The 5 Pro","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-23T18:00:08.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-23T17:29:34.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"IRockSammyProducts"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The new Samsung Watch Ultra may not be for everybody.. but why not??  I suppose if your cornered/jailed in that other fruity ecosystem, or you have an itsy bitsy wrist,  this watch may not be a perfect fit. Otherwise, it checks all of the boxes. \nIt runs Google's and Samsung's latest operating systems, the new watch faces are informative and captivating, the screen face is bright and gorgeous, and the health and wellness information it provides... Just WOW!  And man is it built rugged... Ready for anything outdoors, including the pool or swimming marathons. You can't go wrong with this watch. It should also hold it's value well.  I couldn't be happier with it.","headline":"I Love This Watch and It's Feature Set","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-27T21:35:36.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-01-17T10:36:44.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"CyrilLJ"},"reviewBody":"This is certainly the best watch produced by Samsung. The design is nice, certainly stand out of the market. The performance is also amazing, the animations just feels so refreshing and good. The battery lasts all-day and can definitely do atleast 24hrs without charging. Its so easy to set up as well, easy to connect to my phone and use it (mine is a Samsung). And the watch can definitely stand its test, where the previous ones gained scratches over time, this watch will all the abuse it's recieved still looks brand new.","video":[{"contentUrl":"https://video.api.bazaarvoice.com/4d5537e0-e63d-4f51-ab3d-4b7f0654ff31/video/movie.mp4","thumbnail":{"@type":"ImageObject","name":"BAZAARVOICE"},"uploadDate":"2025-01-17T10:36:44.000+00:00","@type":"VideoObject","name":"4d5537e0-e63d-4f51-ab3d-4b7f0654ff31","description":"Video","thumbnailUrl":"https://video.api.bazaarvoice.com/4d5537e0-e63d-4f51-ab3d-4b7f0654ff31/thumbnail/image-00001.png"}],"headline":"I Love IT","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-02-19T16:45:13.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-17T06:13:09.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Insitu"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The **Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra** is the real deal for anyone who wants a smartwatch that can handle anything. It’s made of titanium, super tough, and has a screen that looks amazing, even in direct sunlight. Plus, it’s super fast—no lag at all—and the battery lasts forever (up to 5 days if you don’t go crazy with notifications!).\n\nThe best part? It’s packed with features: heart rate monitoring, blood oxygen tracking, and even sleep analysis. If you’re into fitness, it’s your ultimate workout buddy with tons of exercise modes, and it’s water- and dust-resistant like a champ. Sure, it’s a bit pricey, but if you want a watch that does it all, this is your go-to.","headline":"The best smart watch ever","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-29T16:37:43.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-29T16:05:40.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"TWHL"},"reviewBody":"After trying for over a week and going back and fourth between Tmobile and Samsung,  my watch ultra is finally activated as a standalone watch! Both Tmobile and Samsung need to figure out a more efficient way to allow the watch to operate as standalone. Samsung says the watch is standalone, Tmobile continues to tell customers no Samsung watch manufactured after 2018 will work as standalone ( yet they advertise standalone plans). Anywhere, Tmobile finally figured it out and my watch now fully functions as standalone ( as it should, as advertised). I am enjoying the watch, thus far. Samsung, please have a meeting with Tmobile","headline":"Updated Review","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-30T01:45:11.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-10-30T01:20:37.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Gowda007"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The Galaxy Watch Ultra impresses with its rugged design, excellent build quality, and comprehensive health-tracking features, making it a strong choice for fitness enthusiasts and adventurers. It offers an extended battery life, bright and responsive AMOLED display, and advanced GPS capabilities, making it ideal for outdoor use. The interface is smooth and user-friendly, integrating well with Samsung's ecosystem, while also supporting various third-party apps. However, the watch’s size might feel bulky for some, and it's priced on the higher end, but its performance and durability make it a worthwhile investment for those seeking a premium smartwatch experience","headline":"I just love it","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-01-02T21:27:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T05:16:16.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Beatbreak"},"reviewBody":"The bad, Disappointing battery performance. After just over a month with this watch I'm very disappointed with the battery life, I'm only getting 1 to 1 1/2 days battery life with aod turned off and using stock watch faces. The charging is very slow, over an hour to recharge. The missing spinning bezel was a major design flaw / oversight on Samsung's part. Replacement Samsung bands are ridiculously expensive.\r\n\r\nThe good, The watch operates flawlessly otherwise, snappy and bright. comes in handy controlling my s24 ultra and receiving notifications. Health monitoring has been a huge improvement over my past Samsung watches.","headline":"Design is great, colors are ok, battery sucks","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-25T12:15:08.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-25T11:43:57.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Watchwarrior47"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Having the very first samsung watch to now the Samsung Galaxy Watch 7 Ultra it is a powerful companion for health-conscious individuals. With its advanced heart rate monitoring capabilities, it can accurately track your cardiovascular health throughout the day and night which is great for people who may suffer from atrial fibrillation. Its robust activity tracking features make it ideal for fitness enthusiasts, allowing you to monitor your steps, calories burned, and sleep quality. Plus, its seamless integration with the Galaxy S24 Ultra ensures a cohesive and convenient user experience, providing real-time notifications and data syncing between the two devices.","headline":"Galaxy Titan","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T17:15:18.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T16:54:18.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"WalkAndBikeDC"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] This watch has been great for fitness. I mostly run and bike so the improved GPS has been a plus. Recognizes my location way faster. I love the look of the watch. Not too big for my wrist and I chose the more understated grey/black color bands.\n\nOnly disappointment was that the case was scratched within a week of my purchase. I'm not even sure when it happened, but I was surprised as the case is supposed to be titanium. Also some of the orange paint was chipped on the face. This has not hindered the use of the watch but if I were doing more rugged sports, I suppose it'd be a badge of honor. But as a casual athlete, I wish it had resisted scratching more readily.","headline":"Love the look! Scratched too easily","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2025-07-01T14:45:11.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-06-30T22:21:51.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"ItswatchU4me"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I love my Samsung Galaxy watch ultra. I always upgrade to the flagship model each year. I wasn't sure that I would like giving up the rotating bezel from the classic series last year but surprisingly I haven't missed it. I do love that this model is different and distinctive and I'm often asked about it in public. I do love the watch band class or pin system. It's very convenient for someone like me who changes watch bands almost daily. I love having all of my health information integrated so that I can see everything at a glance. Getting set up for workouts and auto detection features work flawlessly I have no complaints.","headline":"Love the style and feature set","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-12T19:30:17.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-12T19:04:25.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Hebro50"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Coming from the watch4 44mm,  I knew that the galaxy watch 7ultra would be an up grade, but oh my, this watch blew my sock of and is still impressing me, especially with the AI in the health and fitness. The cushion case is a breath of fresh air. I hope you have a patent on this lug system, it's the best ever made, no pins to scratch the inner lugs, and so much easier to change out, samsung went above and beyond on making this watch. Can't forget about the titanium casing, it's classy and rugged at the same time, you slap a on marine band to do your out door stuff,  or go out on the town with a trail band. Over all with the AI samsung has built a master piece. 👍","headline":"This watch blew my socks off.","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-20T04:21:31.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-04T13:04:45.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Karim"},"reviewBody":"Do not waste your money on the Galaxy Watch Ultra. This so-called \"premium\" smartwatch is nothing but an overpriced piece of garbage. The battery life is absolutely terrible—it barely lasts a day on a full charge. And to make matters worse, it takes a ridiculous 4 hours to charge back up.\n\nThe health tracking features? Completely unreliable. The heart rate monitor, sleep tracker, and other health options are far from accurate, making them pretty much useless. If you're expecting a smartwatch that can actually help with fitness tracking, look elsewhere.\n\nSamsung really dropped the ball with this one. Save yourself the frustration and invest in a better alternative.","headline":"A Complete Waste of Money","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":1}},{"datePublished":"2024-12-26T11:20:38.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-01T15:35:35.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Anonymous"},"reviewBody":"I received my Galaxy 7 ultra watch and was very excited. It's a beuatiful watch and I did have problems with it when I used some of it's features. I have several tattoos on my arms and the heart rate monitor won't work it always tells me to scoot the watch down. No matter how many times I do this it won't work. When I go to use the tutorial for the gestures it keeps telling me to put watch on when I clearly have it on. I really hope yall can fix this and I didn't waste money on this expensive watch and not be able to use all the features. I put the watch on my wife who has no tattoos on her arm and the watch worked fine.","headline":"Doesn't work with tattoos","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":1}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-03T21:30:19.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-06-02T21:10:21.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Willard"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Samsung has redefined what a premium smartwatch can be with the Galaxy Watch Ultra—a rugged, intelligent, and beautifully crafted wearable that doesn’t just track time, but enhances your life in subtle, powerful ways. Blending premium design with cutting-edge performance and AI-enhanced features, this watch is a serious contender in the world of ultra-smart wearables. What truly sets the Watch Ultra apart is its integration with Galaxy AI, Samsung’s new on-device artificial intelligence engine. This is not just AI for show—it’s seamlessly woven into the experience, improving utility, personalization, and daily insights.","headline":"Excellent product","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-11-26T04:00:03.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-11-26T02:30:45.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"ATL69"},"reviewBody":"I had the Watch 6 classic prior to this, and I was nervous reading some of the reviews regarding battery life.  My watch 6 only really ever got a day, maybe a day and a half of use, so I was skeptical this would last.  I'm happy to say the other reviews weren't correct, and the battery life in the Ultra is amazing.  I get 3 days with regular use before I have to charge it.  Overall, this is a great watch, however, I'm giving it 4 stars, due to not getting full functionality unless you also have a Samsung phone.  I have a Sony Xperia, and the amount I spent on this watch, I should get full functionality.  So be warned if you have anything other than a Samsung phone.","headline":"Great battery life.","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-14T23:00:05.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-10-14T22:42:03.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"cano14"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] In my professional opinion, as a seasoned user of various fitness tracking devices, I must commend the Samsung Ultra for its exceptional features. The accuracy of its tracking capabilities, particularly in monitoring energy levels, is truly remarkable. Unlike other brands that I have tried, which provided inconsistent sleep tracking data, the Samsung Ultra stands out for its precision. This has undoubtedly made me a loyal Samsung enthusiast, surpassing my previous admiration for other brands. Samsung has truly excelled with the Ultra, delivering a device that combines style, color, and exceptional tracking capabilities.","headline":"Best watch ever!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-12T20:15:12.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-12T19:55:47.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Watchdude"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I really like this watch. Mostly because it looks cool. The look of this watch makes up for it's few weaknesses; for example it's not comfortable. It also won't charge on a flat charger like my Samsung Trio. However, because it looks so cool, I'm OK with the discomfort and the inconvenience. It also had AI. The AI comes in real handy, when you need it. I love the big screen, typing of a watch was never easy, but on the Ultra, it is very easy. I like the new extra button, it's nice to quickly start mr workout. The orange is very sophisticated. I like knowing it's super durable,  I don't feel like I need to be careful,  I just do am live and I'm confident it'll be OK.","headline":"This watch is cool","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-06-11T12:45:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-06-10T18:56:30.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Glow8Gurl"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I originally purchased this watch for tracking my sleep and measure my body composition, but I didn't know how much easier it would be to communicate and be able to answer calls when I'm away from my phone and see messages and determine whether or not they need to be answered right away or not. I can be away from my phone for long periods of time, so it's good that I can see my day notifications. Galaxy AI makes it so easy for me to do touch free or communicate touch free when im getting my hands dirty or just dont want to get my phone to do it.  I love my watch and I think I'm going to keep it around for a long time.","headline":"Everything about it is perfect","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-02-11T23:30:11.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-11T20:56:07.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Androidfaithful"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I have very labor intensive work daily.\nI purchased this device to be able to track my physical activity while staying connected to my family & important information I would normally receive on my phone.....\nMy 1st task upon purchased was to include screen protectors, case protection, etc.  anticipating potential damage because of my work.\nWell aside from All of my preparation for disaster; I have dropped, stepped on, & all but submerged this watch in fire & ice, and I tell you, not even a hiccup.\nFrom complete skeptic, to total believer.\nPurchased bands for every occasion and literally is the only item I wear daily.","headline":"The durability of this product is very impressive","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2025-08-25T02:30:05.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-08-07T18:47:41.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Karah"},"reviewBody":"I bought this mainly for the longer charge this watch holds, compared to my older Galaxy Watch 6 that would run out the battery in less than a day. The new Galaxy Watch Ultra lasts me almost 2 days (depending on if I use it for working out or not) before having to charge it again! The only downfall is just how bulky it is, so when I do do exercises that has me down on my hands, if my wrist bends at all, it will hit the main button and it has stopped my workout session early. This has happened a couple times now, so I usually slide it down my arm a little when I do those exercises. It's just annoying, but not a deal breaker for me. Overall, very happy with my purchase!!","headline":"Awesome battery power & lots of features!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-05T17:00:19.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-04T04:44:35.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Chevyrida79"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] So let's start with the software and how smooth it is. Very snappy and responsive. I must say that I'm actually impressed with the watch faces from Samsung. I truly hope they continue to produce more watch faces because they are amazing. I love the ability to customize the faces even down to a granular level. The screen size is perfect, the build is substantial, the feel of the watch on my wrist if perfect. If your coming from any of the classics it's does feel like an upgrade. I miss the rotating bezel but honestly it's not a deal breaker for me. I'm actually excited to wear my watch again. This is not just another incremental update it's a major change and I love it.","headline":"Way better in person!!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-26T22:15:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-26T21:47:03.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jbald111"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I am very impressed with my Galaxy Watch Ultra.   Battery life is exceptional,  and I think it's the best looking Galaxy watch yet. \nThe AI aspect of the watch is next level and the health sensors are remarkable. \nI can do an EEG, step counting is accurate,   a close blood OX reading,  heart rate,  and a lot more I haven't had a chance to check out. \nI currently only use my watch by Bluetooth connecting with my phone but when I can pay for the data plan will be excited about stand alone calls with my watch only. \nOver all I think this watch is worth the money.   \nI wear it all day and night.   \n\nVery happy customer!","headline":"Best looking with the best tech watch","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T18:00:13.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T17:41:15.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sephy76"},"reviewBody":"I just get mine yesterdayand overall to me the weight is perfect I have big hands and I can text on this one, I trade I. The 5 pro and this one is 10 time better, the battery last right now in my second day and still have 50% I didn't ajust nothing so the battery las a lot.... play a bit with faces love it, audio is strong, the alarm ia crazy loud, the brightness is to strong some times but you can see the screen perfectly on day light, the watch bands this time are large enough for me.... the temperature sensor works too, the action button can be better but for now I just set the flashlight in double tap, perfect for night if you wake up, is the perfect watch....10/10","headline":"THE WATCH....","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-02-11T21:00:12.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-11T20:37:49.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"3Bclover"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The Galaxy Ultra Watch has it all! I am impressed with how seamless and fluid it is to transition from one app to the other or when I'm exercising how easy it is to choose what I'm doing. Along with the ease of setting controls, I love the quick button. I have mine set for running when double pressed so I can start sooner. The face of the Watch is also a plus not to big and not to small. I can text or swipe text with ease. The volume is excellent as well when I'm on call and or just listing to my favorite podcast, I'm not struggling to hear what is being said. Overall  im very satisfied with the Galaxy Watch Ultra.","headline":"My Galaxy Ultra Watch Review!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-31T23:17:12.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T21:17:14.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jddd221"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] This watch does have great features that i yet have to explore.  But there are some otems i would change. I was not a fan of the round screen as i feel to much screen is lost due to this. The round bezel on top is no longer spinnable which was kind of a bummer. I feel like the orange main button should be customizable instead of just having it for working out. I also feel like the sleep sensor is a little worse then the previous i was able to get better reading on my old watch. I did like the function of more possibilities of apps. The color itself is nice wpuld have loved a olive green style more this seems as a derivative of the competition.  Overall its an okay watch","headline":"Pros and Cons","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3}},{"datePublished":"2024-10-31T22:45:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-10-29T20:14:52.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Willow"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I'm new to smart watches. I began my my first journey with the Samsung Ultra watch just a few months ago. I have to say I enjoy all Samsung products. Yet this watch is so helpful in more ways than one, two, or three because it has light weight feel plus durability. Functions are easy to navigate and the docent watch faces are brilliantly innovative with design and smart technology. One of my favorites is the ability to support endangered animals. for the support they give you a watch face which I wear proudly. So many functions. And programming is as easy because I can do it from my phone also.  Thank you Samsung🫡","headline":"My ultra watch","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-09-16T21:00:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-16T11:48:05.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Magick20"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The watch finally arrived last week. Have been testing back and forth. These are the finding I found about it:-\n\nPROS\n+ Nice Big Display\n+ Battery life amazingly good\n+ Calling and Messaging , very easy to pair up with my phone and also use as a standalone phone on the go\n\nThe Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra is a watch available right now if you require full WearOS platform access, excellent GPS accuracy, and a longer battery life. In terms of training heart rate, it's a little hit or miss (maybe it was me). When I ran and rode indoors, I found it to be fairly accurate. Overall satisfied and would recommend this watch.","headline":"Samsung Galaxy Smart Watch 7 Ultra","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-15T10:32:47.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-12T11:11:30.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Gordon163"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I have had the Galaxy Ultra for a week now and i am really impressed with its performance .\nThe first thing i noticed when i opened the box was the build quality which is really impressive.The watch has so many options to personalise the watch faces and functions.\nI like using my watch to track my fitness and sleep which the ultra does with great accuracy.\nThe only negative with the Ultra is it doesn't have the rotating bezel which is on the Galaxy 6 watch.This is a minor thing though.All in I would  recommend  the ultra to anyone that is interested in keeping an eye on their fitness progress and quality of sleep","headline":"Excellent Smart Watch","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-09-06T02:00:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-04T16:20:17.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"ViperN226"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The battery life has absolutely amazed me going from my galaxy watch 4 classic I had no idea what I was missing. I only ever charge the watch when I shower and it is always above 50%. if you are worried about it being an inconvenience to charge do not worry. the amount of features always surprises me on my watch, from my detailed sleep patterns so the large variety of workouts that you can select. the watch frame is also very strong. I have nicked it on many surfaces to find that there are still no scratches or dents at all but on the other objects like the desk I bumped it on.I am very impressed with this watch.","headline":"Amazing battery life and great features","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-30T16:00:31.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-30T07:08:30.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"BigLA23"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] PLEASE STAY AWAY!  If you own Galaxy Watch 4 or later, DO NOT UPGRADE if you like watch face NOT from samsung. Even \"Galaxy AI\" is not worth upgrading for and a total disappointment. This new watch will not let you use the same watch faces you have been using, even if you have used the same faces on every watch since Watch Active 2. And Galaxy AI is a joke. It's the same thing you get on older models with the updated OS. I would say upgrade if you own Watch 3 or earlier, but even then, go to the Watch 5 Pro. I'm regretting the trade in. Also, the square dial is GARBAGE. If we wanted a square watch, we would get another brand watch. If you upgrade, you WILL be disappointed","headline":"Worst Watch Upgrade","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-30T10:38:54.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-28T13:11:09.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Anonymous"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The Samsung watch ultra is big, bold and feature packed. \nI have had my watch 5 pro for a couple of years now and was wary the ultra would be too big in comparison but it really is about the same (I have a case on the pro) so I was pleasantly surprised.\nI am getting 2 days with the always on mode and 4/5 with raise to wake.\nThe screen is clear and easy to use and set up quick and simple. \nThe auto tracking features so far seem to work great as it has picked up on all the walks I have been on so far. \nI would highly recommend this watch to anyone who wants great battery life and an amazing workout health tracker.","headline":"Great upgrade for the Samsung ecosystem","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-05-22T15:39:37.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-05-16T17:43:12.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Liam P"},"reviewBody":"This watch is incredible. It does everything I wanted it to do very well. Mileage while running and walking is pretty accurate just from what I've measured, heart rate while working out on weight machines at the gym is always spot on. Battery life is great at 3 days (including sleep tracking). The device gets warm while charging, but the small magnetic wireless charger is sweet. I only wish it had a usb-c port on it instead of having a cable come out of it.\n\nMy only complaints are that is is a thick boy, it's stand off of my wrist much taller than a regular analog watch. Also, the included strap isn't terrible comfortable, and also bulky. And replacement straps are pricey.","headline":"Everything I needed it to be and more","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-11-15T02:23:20.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-22T14:31:47.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"John"},"reviewBody":"The Watch Ultra needs to show correct swim laps when exercising in the pool.\nI do 74 laps, and it takes around 50-55 minutes. I compared it with Watch6 (the same result for 74 laps done—the watch showed only 48 and 52 - it doesn't show all laps) and another brand (the watch showed all the laps I swam—perfect count of the laps), so it is about 30% incorrect, way too much.\nIt happened after the last update.\nAlso, the reading of the calories for Watch6 and Watch Ultra are different.\nIt is unacceptable for such an expensive watch to show the results of exercise with such big differences.\n Please correct the problem.","headline":"Exercises problem","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":2}},{"datePublished":"2024-08-12T21:30:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-12T21:14:57.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ultrauser1"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Long-time user of Android/Samsung products, especially when it comes to watches. So I've experienced it from the beginning, and I can say this watch is by far one of my favorites so far. The design is awesome, as well as the battery life! I love how they integrated Galaxy AI into the watch and many other features like sleep score to the action button for workouts! I use this watch every day regardless of the activity. So all in all, there are a lot of improvements and awesome features. I would highly recommend this watch to anyone who enjoys wearing a watch and wants to keep track of their day-to-day activities.","headline":"Galaxy watch ultra","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-01-05T01:44:47.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-26T17:47:45.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"BJMAC"},"reviewBody":"The most \"put together\" samsung watch I have owned.  I have owned several generations since the 2nd gen samsung smarth watch and this is the best.  Definitely better accuracy on GPS and calorie burn, and it finally looks like it can compete withe the style and feel of larger traditional mechanical watches.  I was concerned the screen was a bit too large, but it actually has allowed me to use features like email and message summary which were too small to be useful on previous models.  With Galaxy AI, it feels like the watch ecosystem has turned a corner in terms of user engagement.  Very happy with the purchase!","headline":"Finally a watch that checks all the boxes!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2025-08-30T15:55:51.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-08-29T22:28:05.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"billy2461"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] So, my first impressions of the Samsung Watch Ultra LTE are that I love it! The functions that you are able to tweak, the different faces, and also, I am not a cyclist or runner, but I am an archer, which you can add to the exercises tab. The health benefits of being able to check on blood pressure and ECG as well to help in managing health are great. The apps that are included when downloaded are streamlined and straightforward, adding an LTE data allowance. I can't wait to put the watch through its paces. Now we have Gemini AI installed also, which can help in searches, menu planning, and other tasks. I can't believe I have not had a watch like this before. Over the moon!","headline":"Samsung watch ultra","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-09-15T07:30:04.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-09-15T07:13:22.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jamal"},"reviewBody":"This is definitely the best Galaxy watch yet, I'd argue the best combination smartwatch and fitness device on the market. From a user standpoint, it does everything well. GPS and activity tracking are vastly improved from other iterations I've had (this is my 8th galaxy watch).  I use the LTE feature and call quality and text messaging work flawlessly.  I was really disappointed there was no option for the rotating bezel, still am, but the screen works really well and I've had no real issues with it.  The design grows on you by the day, to the point that it works in any situation.  Classy and sporty.  The GWU is just a comprehensive value buy if you're big in Smart watches.","headline":"Watch ultra winning","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2024-07-31T18:15:08.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-31T17:48:07.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Andyultra"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I have had the galaxy watch 5 pro since that came out and didn't care about a rotating bezel on the 6. I do alot of out door activities so I need a very strong watch.\nThe galaxy watch ultra addresses any issue I had with the 5pro. More accurate sensors for health monitoring. Quick access to workouts with the action button. New GPS, amazing. The way that my ultra works with my phone S23ultra to use Galaxy AI is really impressive as well.  \n\nAlso, the battery life is just as good as my 5pro was. \nNight mode also a great feature on the ultra face. \n\nI could keep going, but to sum it up I really can't think of anything I would change at this point. Really happy with my upgrade.","headline":"Great upgrade from the watch 5 pro","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2026-07-04T23:01:35.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-07-18T10:22:53.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Samsungluver"},"reviewBody":"Saatin fiyatı tam 44 bin lira. Yanlış duymadınız. S24+ telefondan daha pahalı :)","headline":"Harika bir fiyat :)","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":1}},{"datePublished":"2025-07-08T00:00:11.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-07-07T19:26:38.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"GerryFromSalisbury"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] The Galaxy Watch Ultra is amazing! It's actually more watch than I need, but it is so worth it. The first thing I noticed was the band attachment. Great upgrade from previous models. It makes changing bands painless. The face of the watch appears to be bigger, but compared to the 5, it's about the same.The functionality is seamless from one model to the next. The only feature that I haven't been able to achieve was the double pinch to wake the watch up or take a photo. I'm sure I'll get it figured out. Overall, I can always depend on Samsung to have a solid mobile phone and watch. They haven't let me down yet.","headline":"Excellent Purchase","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}},{"datePublished":"2026-04-22T06:09:33.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-08-04T14:13:12.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"akadirturkut"},"reviewBody":"100 metre derinlik var fakat dalış özelliği yok ve bu fiyat ilginç samsung","headline":"ilginç olan Saatin dalış özelliği olmaması","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3}},{"datePublished":"2025-07-09T14:15:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-07-09T13:57:53.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jordanboi5"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] Haha, I'm just a regular user too. And honestly, those features like sleep apnea, sleep time, and heart rate are awesome. But how important are they to you?\n\nI just lift weights and run, so it's cool. The only problem is if you have tattoos, it won't read your heart rate. But, like, that makes sense, right?\n\nI don't have cellular service, but you should totally get it. It's super convenient, especially for running. You can listen to music without your phone.\n\nOh, and it's kinda big, lol, but for me, it's all about what I like.\n\nI wish the watch could announce the quarter times out loud, that would be helpful.","headline":"It works?","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2024-11-15T01:15:09.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2024-11-14T18:06:17.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Rick"},"reviewBody":"Moved up from a Watch 5 Pro.  The 5 Pro was fast, but this Ultra is even faster.  Beautiful display.  Unfortunately, the same issue I saw with the 5 Pro is still present with this model:   it misses most of my floor climbs.  I routinely do 12 - 15 floors every day, but it only records 3 - 4 most days.  Fitbit is much better at recording these accurately.  Other tracking functions appear to be good.  About the same battery life as the 5 Pro, but it seems to charge a little bit more slowly. \n Disappointed that the magnetic clasp band from the 5 Pro wasn't available on the new one.  Had to replace it with a third party product.  Overall an impressive watch and I do recommend it.","headline":"Very nice watch!","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4}},{"datePublished":"2025-02-28T17:00:10.000+00:00","dateCreated":"2025-02-25T22:35:12.000+00:00","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"KNIGHTMare"},"reviewBody":"[This review was collected as part of a promotion.] I got the new galaxy ultra watch and in my opinion this is the best watch I've gotten by far. It doesn't feel too heavy especially when I wear it to bed I don't feel like it's catching onto my pillow or uncomfortable wearing the device, i love the features of it tracking my blood oxygen while I sleep. How long I was in deep sleep, my body temp. I was worried about this watch since it is a ultra, but i was pleasently surprised and the amount of times I've hit this device on the wall or scrapped it I've been so worried about if the device was gonna have cracks or scratches and it still looks as if I just pulled it out of the box. This is by far one my favorite samsung purchases","headline":"Durable beautiful watch","reviewRating":{"bestRating":5,"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5}}],"@id":"https://www.samsung.com/tr/watches/galaxy-watch/galaxy-watch-ultra-titanium-gray-lte-sm-l705fdaatur/","aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"4.7","ratingCount":6054},"@context":"https://schema.org"}
