                <div class="pdd44-review__contents-detail">
                    <div class="pdd44-review__contents-detail-text-wrap">
                        <div class="pdd44-review__contents-detail-text-inner">
                            <div class="pdd44-review__contents-detail-text">The watch is pretty much the Galaxy Watch 7 in a different case with an action button. It&#39;s advertised as a tough and rugged version of outdoor sports. Suddenly, one day, the sensors stopped functioning, and then the action button wasn&#39;t responding; I am now facing repair costs because it is considered out of warranty for some unseen internal damage. There is no cracked screen, no scratches or nicks. It&#39;s never been dropped and slammed against anything, yet somehow, there is damage to the motherboard. I am quickly getting fed up with Samsung, trying to avoid costs at my expense. 

So think twice if you invest in this watch for its rugged, tough case.</div>
                        </div>
