                    <div class="pdd44-review__contents-detail-text-wrap">
                        <div class="pdd44-review__contents-detail-text-inner">
                            <div class="pdd44-review__contents-detail-text">I’m upgrading from a Galaxy Watch 6 Classic. I bought the watch as I wanted more battery life and this watch does not disappoint. Mine shipped with firmware version AXFB and I’m getting 48 hours with BT on, WiFi and LTE on Auto AND AOD on.

The software is also way snappier with no lag.

Also the vibration motor got a big upgrade. It feels sort of like a PS5 Dual Sense Controller vs an N64 Rumble pack on the previous watch.

Lastly, I like the new band attachment system. It provides a loud positive click confirming that the band is fully seated unlike the vagueness that can sometimes happen with the usual watch band pin system.</div>
                        </div>
