                    <div class="pdd44-review__contents-response-body">
                        <p class="pdd44-review__contents-response-body-title">R&amp;R Team</p>
                        <p class="pdd44-review__contents-response-body-text">Hi there Karim, 
Thanks for sharing your experience with using your Galaxy Watch Ultra. Your feedback is valuable as we continue our journey to bring our consumers the best in design and functionality. The Galaxy Watch Ultra offers up to 100 hours of battery life when in Power saving mode, up to 48 hours in Exercise power saving mode, and up to 60 hours of battery life without Power Saving mode. This is based on typical usage so results may vary. There are several reasons why your Galaxy Watch may be experiencing battery drain or have decreased battery life. For instance, certain apps can increase battery consumption. Please take a moment to review, &#34;Reduced battery life on your Samsung smart watch&#34; when you have the available time to learn about how you can increase your watch battery life. Also check out, &#34;Clear the app cache and data on your Galaxy phone or tablet&#34; and &#34;Use Samsung Health sleep monitoring on your Galaxy Watch&#34; to help resolve what you have described to be experiencing with your health tracking features. I have also included the link to your device manual for your review. Let us know if you have any questions for us after checking those out by reaching out to Samsung Support. We&#39;d be happy to assist you further. Thank you for choosing Samsung!
- Debra 

